From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:19:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Stop the trade block-request timer when the section ends

TradeConnection arms m_commandRequestTimer for 2 s at several points and never
stops it. When the section is destroyed with the timer still armed (a cancel,
or a partner who left mid-block), the k_timer -- which Zephyr keeps linked in
its timeout list -- is freed stack memory: the expiry runs on a dead object,
and the frame's reuse corrupts the list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014LvpUYFw94JkaNFyrbwJmK
---
 src/sections/tradeConnection.hpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sections/tradeConnection.hpp b/src/sections/tradeConnection.hpp
index 7759d68..268c1bf 100644
--- a/src/sections/tradeConnection.hpp
+++ b/src/sections/tradeConnection.hpp
@@ -36,6 +36,10 @@ public:
     ~TradeConnection()
     {
         while(!m_packetLayer.idle()) {};
+        // The 2 s request timer can still be armed when the section ends; the
+        // k_timer is a node in the kernel's timeout list and lives in this
+        // object, so it must be stopped before the object goes away.
+        k_timer_stop(&m_commandRequestTimer);
     }
 
     NextSection process() override;
